  "worked_solution": "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-14t+5 & =5 \\\\ {t}^{2}-14t & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-2\\cdot t\\cdot 7+{7}^{2}-{7}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (t-7{)}^{2}-{7}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (t-7{)}^{2} & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=-7$ and $q=49.$ Thus, $pq=-343.$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-7{)}^{2} & =49 \\\\ \\sqrt{(t-7{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ |t-7| & =7 \\\\ t-7 & =\\pm 7 \\\\ t & =7\\pm 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =7-7=0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =7+7=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum is ${t}_{1}+{t}_{2}=14.$",
